% Steensgaard's analysis (1996): where Andersen's says p = q makes what
% q points to included in what p points to, this makes the two equal.
% Coarser, and in its hand-written form almost linear. Run with
% instructions.dl:
%   same(A, B)        A and B point to the same things
%   pt(V, H), call_edge(I, F)   as in andersen.dl, always its superset
%
%     p = &a;  q = &b;  p = q;        Andersen's: q -> b only
%                                     here: p, q -> a, b, and a is b
%
% Fields are by name (x.f one place for every x): an object's fields
% unified would need a term for "the contents of the contents". So
% store and load are through a place F, which same then unifies.
%
% design:
% Not fast here. Its speed comes from a union-find, each set one node,
% and same/2 writes every pair of each set out instead: quadratic in
% the size of a class. It is here because it says what the difference
% with Andersen's is, in rules: drop the symmetry of same and of a
% copy, and you are back to inclusion.
%
% cs-history:
% Bjarne Steensgaard, at Microsoft Research, wanted an alias analysis
% for millions of lines, on machines of 1996; it ran where Andersen's
% then could not. Manuvir Das's One Level Flow (2000) kept its speed
% with most of Andersen's precision on C, by unifying only below the
% first level. The trade off of precision against time never closed:
% the analyses here are points along it.
%
% References: Bjarne Steensgaard, "Points-to analysis in almost linear
% time" (POPL 1996); Manuvir Das, "Unification-based pointer analysis
% with directional assignments" (PLDI 2000).

same(P, Q) :- copy(P, Q).
same(Q, P) :- same(P, Q).
same(A, C) :- same(A, B), same(B, C).

pt(V, H) :- alloc(V, H).
pt(V, H) :- same(V, W), alloc(W, H).

% two things one pointer may point to hold the same
same(H, K) :- pt(V, H), pt(V, K).

% star, and fields by name: a place of its own, unified with what goes in
same(P, H) :- load(P, X, star), pt(X, H).
same(V, H) :- store(X, star, V), pt(X, H).
same(P, F) :- load(P, _, F), F \= star.
same(V, F) :- store(_, F, V), F \= star.
pt(P, F) :- assign_field_address(P, _, F).

call_edge(I, F) :- call_direct(I, F).
call_edge(I, F) :- call_indirect(I, V), pt(V, F), function(F).
same(P, A) :- call_edge(I, F), parameter(F, Z, P), argument(I, Z, A).
same(R, V) :- call_edge(I, F), return(F, V), call_ret(I, R).
